From 9756b8a6395df3008312410b57601514d3c317f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreyansh Kaushik <smkaushi@ucsc.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:21:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] macOS: native trackpad, Cmd shortcuts and shared clipboard
 for Lightpath hosts

Keyboard
- Always send Cmd (and the Meta modifier) so the host can map Mac shortcuts
  (Cmd+C, Cmd+Tab, ...) to Linux ones; /launch and /resume carry
  lightpathClient=mac so the host knows to.
- While the keyboard is captured, swap in an empty main menu so Cmd+Q, Cmd+H,
  Cmd+W, Cmd+M reach the host instead of quitting or hiding Moonlight
  (re-applied before each Cmd key in case Qt reinstalls its menu).

Trackpad (AppKit event monitor, main thread)
- Precise scrolling (trackpad, Magic Mouse) is sent 1:1 as 12 units per
  point, unclamped, including macOS momentum, split into int16 chunks; mouse
  wheel notches become 60 points.
- Pinch = Ctrl+wheel steps, two-finger double tap = Ctrl+0, three-finger page
  swipe = Cmd+[ / Cmd+] (the host maps them to Back/Forward). macOS
  Spaces/Mission Control gestures untouched.

Clipboard
- Synced when moving between Mac and stream (no polling): the Mac copy is
  sent when the stream window gains focus, the PC copy fetched when it loses
  focus and when the stream ends (waits at most 500 ms). Text and images
  (PNG, TIFF converted), up to 16 MiB, over the paired HTTPS channel
  (GET/POST /lightpath/clipboard, new POST support in NvHTTP). Transfers run
  in order on one worker thread; echo suppression, stale-result and
  "Mac copied meanwhile" checks; hosts answering 404 turn it off.

Pure logic lives in trackpad.h / ClipboardSyncState with a standalone test
(tests/lightpath/lightpath_input_test.cpp).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSGYnegbZ8CEyDK2p2YTH2
